1
00:00:03,052 --> 00:00:06,080
When Mila breathes on the mirror, it fogs up!

2
00:00:06,130 --> 00:00:08,200
And Noah takes a big breath in…

3
00:00:08,250 --> 00:00:09,823
but what do we breathe?

4
00:00:10,612 --> 00:00:12,387
Noah catches air in a bag.

5
00:00:12,437 --> 00:00:14,001
You can't see anything,

6
00:00:14,051 --> 00:00:15,686
and yet the bag is full!

7
00:00:15,736 --> 00:00:18,894
Mila presses, and it pushes back: air exists!

8
00:00:19,662 --> 00:00:21,176
Discovery mission!

9
00:00:23,692 --> 00:00:24,243
Mini mode!

10
00:00:24,293 --> 00:00:25,565
Air is a mix of gases…

11
00:00:25,615 --> 00:00:29,171
out of one hundred balls of air, seventy-eight are nitrogen,

12
00:00:29,221 --> 00:00:32,406
twenty-one are oxygen, and a handful are other gases.

13
00:00:33,208 --> 00:00:36,524
When you breathe in, the air goes down into your lungs,

14
00:00:36,574 --> 00:00:37,442
into tiny sacs.

15
00:00:37,492 --> 00:00:39,952
There, the oxygen passes into your blood,

16
00:00:40,002 --> 00:00:42,573
which brings back a waste: carbon dioxide.

17
00:00:43,340 --> 00:00:46,828
And when you breathe out, a little less oxygen comes out,

18
00:00:46,878 --> 00:00:48,628
a little more carbon dioxide…

19
00:00:48,678 --> 00:00:49,621
and water vapor.

20
00:00:49,671 --> 00:00:51,472
That's the fog on the mirror!

21
00:00:52,270 --> 00:00:56,423
With oxygen, your body burns food to make energy.

22
00:00:56,473 --> 00:00:57,881
But who makes it?

23
00:00:57,931 --> 00:01:00,332
Plants, so thank you, trees!

24
00:01:01,131 --> 00:01:02,808
And that's what we breathe.

25
00:01:04,689 --> 00:01:05,901
Air is a mix of gases;

26
00:01:05,951 --> 00:01:09,681
your body keeps the oxygen and lets out carbon dioxide and water.

27
00:01:10,630 --> 00:01:13,444
With an adult: breathe on a cold mirror.

28
00:01:13,494 --> 00:01:16,236
This fog is the water from your breath…

29
00:01:16,286 --> 00:01:18,004
count how long it stays!

30
00:01:18,771 --> 00:01:21,509
And why do leaves change color in autumn?

31
00:01:21,559 --> 00:01:22,919
The answer tomorrow.
